      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This error shows up in both logs as the only thing that would prevent a world from loading:\n\n```\n\n2026.07.11 22:16:26 Error      -  [NetworkProcessing] Failed to configure network IDs on Trigger (40)\n\n2026.07.11 22:16:26 Error      -  [NetworkProcessing] Cannot use ID 8033 as it's already in use on /Tiharuum/GlobalObjectActive_Game/30-Yavalath/Yavalath (1)/Triggers/Trigger (37)\n\n```\n\nThis is on world `wrld_e8db4bf4-9da9-4dd4-9dc3-1cd56820f038`. The issue is not something we can fix, the world itself has corrupt network IDs. If this is your world, you can use the Network ID Utility in the VRChat SDK to fix this issue and reupload. If this is your home world, it may lead to some looping before falling back to VRChat's Default Home.",
